>
  <h1>Costa Rica Credentials</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    The <code>cr-vc-sdk</code> extends the base VC SDK with Costa Rica-specific
    credential types. Combined with <code>cr-vc-schemas</code> for JSON-LD contexts.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="Terminal">
<Fragment set:html={`npm install <span class="c-str">@attestto-com/cr-vc-sdk</span> <span class="c-str">@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Available credential types</h2>
  <p>The following CR-specific credential types are supported:</p>

  <ul style="color: var(--docs-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 2; padding-left: 1.5rem;">
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">DrivingLicense</strong> — Costa Rica driver's license with license class, restrictions, and validity.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">TheoreticalTestResult</strong> — Driving theory exam result with score, passing threshold, and exam center.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">MedicalCertificate</strong> — Medical fitness certificate for driving or professional licensing.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">VehicleInspection</strong> — RTV (Revisi&oacute;n T&eacute;cnica Vehicular) inspection result with pass/fail and findings.</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">ProfessionalLicense</strong> — Colegio-issued professional license (engineering, medicine, law, etc.).</li>
    <li><strong style="color: var(--docs-text);">IdentityCredential</strong> — C&eacute;dula-based identity attestation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Schema plugins</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas</code> package provides a <code>SchemaPlugin</code>
    for each credential type. Each plugin injects the correct JSON-LD context URI.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Available schema plugins">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  drivingLicenseSchema,
  theoreticalTestSchema,
  medicalCertSchema,
  vehicleInspectionSchema,
  professionalLicenseSchema,
  identityCredentialSchema,
<span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas'</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Issuing a DrivingLicense</h2>
  <p>Full example using <code>cr-vc-sdk</code> with the driving license schema:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="issue-driving-license.ts">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCIssuer, generateKeyPair <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/cr-vc-sdk'</span>
<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> drivingLicenseSchema <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>()

<span class="c-kw">const</span> issuer = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCIssuer</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  did: <span class="c-str">'did:web:cosevi.go.cr'</span>,
  privateKey: keys.privateKey,
<span class="c-br">}</span>).<span class="c-fn">use</span>(drivingLicenseSchema)

<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'DrivingLicense'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:holder.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    fullName: <span class="c-str">'Maria Rodriguez Vargas'</span>,
    licenseClass: <span class="c-str">'B1'</span>,
    restrictions: [],
    issueDate: <span class="c-str">'2026-03-15'</span>,
    expiryDate: <span class="c-str">'2032-03-15'</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
  expirationDate: <span class="c-str">'2032-03-15T23:59:59Z'</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(vc[<span class="c-str">'@context'</span>])
<span class="c-cm">// ['https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1', 'https://schemas.attestto.com/cr/driving-license/v1']</span>

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(vc.type)
<span class="c-cm">// ['VerifiableCredential', 'DrivingLicense']</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Issuing a TheoreticalTestResult</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="issue-test-result.ts">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> theoreticalTestSchema <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas'</span>

issuer.<span class="c-fn">use</span>(theoreticalTestSchema)

<span class="c-kw">const</span> testResult = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'TheoreticalTestResult'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:student.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    score: <span class="c-num">87</span>,
    passingThreshold: <span class="c-num">80</span>,
    passed: <span class="c-kw">true</span>,
    examCenter: <span class="c-str">'COSEVI San Jose'</span>,
    examDate: <span class="c-str">'2026-04-10'</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>cr-vc-sdk vs vc-sdk</h2>
  <p>
    The <code>cr-vc-sdk</code> package re-exports everything from <code>vc-sdk</code> and adds
    CR-specific convenience methods. You can use either package — the difference is that
    <code>cr-vc-sdk</code> includes CR type definitions out of the box.
  </p>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>Full type definitions.</strong> For the complete list of properties on each
    credential type, see the
    <a href="https://spec.attestto.com/cr-vc-schemas/" target="_blank">CR VC Schemas specification</a>.
  </Callout>

